elaine: added this short py block:```py
# async streaming
async with client.stream_responses(model='short-v1', input='Summarize errors') as s:
    async for ev in s:
        if ev.type == 'delta':
            print(ev.delta.text)
        elif ev.type == 'done':
            print('done')
    await s.wait_for_completion()
```

raj: Go pattern should show context usage. people forget to cancel.

elaine: go example added:```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 15*time.Second)
defer cancel()
stream, err := client.StreamResponses(ctx, &StreamParams{Model: "short-v1", Input: "Summarize"})
if err != nil { log.Fatal(err) }
for {
    msg, err := stream.Recv()
    if err == io.EOF { break }
    if err != nil { log.Printf("err: %v", err); break }
    if msg.Type == DeltaMessage { fmt.Print(msg.Delta.Text) }
}
stream.Close()
```

